  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Changes to `ranges.mjs`\n\nI rewrote `mergeRanges(ranges)` to fix all the bugs in the original and meet the spec:\n\n**Validation (rejects malformed input with `TypeError`):**\n- Non-array input → `TypeError`\n- Each element must be an array of exactly length 2 → `TypeError`\n- Both bounds must be safe integers (`Number.isSafeInteger`) → `TypeError`\n- `start <= end` enforced → `TypeError`\n\n**Correct merging:**\n- **No input mutation:** validation builds a fresh `pairs` array of new `[start, end]` copies, so the original array and its pairs are never touched. The sort operates on the copy.\n- **Sort by start, then end:** `a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]`.\n- **Adjacency:** merge condition is `start <= last[1] + 1`, so `[2,4]` and `[5,7]` merge into `[2,7]`.\n- **Contained intervals don't shorten:** the end is only extended when `end > last[1]`, so a contained interval like `[3,4]` inside `[1,10]` leaves the end at `10`.\n- **Fresh output:** the result array and every pair in it are newly allocated.\n- **Empty input returns `[]`.**\n\n**Preserved:** the named export `mergeRanges`.\n\nThe two provided tests pass:\n- `mergeRanges([[8,10],[1,3],[2,5]])` → `[[1,5],[8,10]]`\n- `mergeRanges([[5,7],[2,4]])` → `[[2,7]]`",
